%%HP: T(3)A(D)F(.);
@ Installer: creates the TOTP directory (if missing), enters it and stores
@   TZ    UTC offset in hours (France: 2 in summer, 1 in winter)
@   UNIX  Unix time in whole seconds
@   CNT   TOTP counter, floor(UNIX / 30)
@   LEFT  seconds left in the current 30 s window
@ UNIX re-reads DATE until it is stable, so a call across midnight
@ cannot pair the new day with the old time.
\<<
  IFERR 'TOTP' CRDIR THEN END
  TOTP
  2 'TZ' STO
  \<< 0 0 \-> d t
    \<<
      DO DATE 'd' STO TIME 't' STO UNTIL DATE d SAME END
      1.011970 d DDAYS 86400 * t HMS\-> 3600 * + TZ 3600 * - IP
    \>>
  \>> 'UNIX' STO
  \<< UNIX 30 / IP \>> 'CNT' STO
  \<< 30 UNIX 30 MOD - \>> 'LEFT' STO
\>>
